  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Tyson Foods obligated $226M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Tyson Foods received 50 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $4.5M. Obligations are down 0.3% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show a history of higher and lower procurement activity: FY21 was $95.6M, FY22 was $239M, FY23 was $221M, FY24 was $238M, FY25 was $227M, and FY26 is $226M. The current-year total is partial and reflects fiscal year to date obligations. Use the award count and average award size to assess purchase frequency and typical contract scale when planning capture or compliance activities. The year-over-year change signals near stability rather than a large shift in federal demand. Keep in mind that the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables report total contract values rather than contract obligations, and that current-year totals are not full-year results.",
